<title>SPAIN: Spain May CPI rose 1.5 pct yr/yr, up 0.1 pct m/m.</title>
<headline>Spain May CPI rose 1.5 pct yr/yr, up 0.1 pct m/m.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-06-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Statistics Institute (INE) gave the following figures:</p>
<p> SPANISH INFLATION		MAY 97    APR 97   MAY 96</p>
<p> Monthly CPI index change	0.1	 0.0	0.3</p>
<p> Year-on-year rise		 1.5	 1.7	3.8</p>
<p> Core inflation		    0.1	 0.1	0.1</p>
<p> Year-on-year rise		 1.9	 1.9	3.7</p>
<p> INDEX BY COMPONENTS	     MAY 97     APR 97     YR/YR</p>
<p> Food				   0.1	 -0.2	 -0.6</p>
<p> Clothing			     0.2	  0.4	  2.0</p>
<p> Housing				0.2	  0.2	  3.1</p>
<p> Household goods		    0.1	  0.2	  1.7</p>
<p> Medicine			     0.5	  0.3	  3.1</p>
<p> Transport			    0.1	  0.0	  1.8</p>
<p> Culture				0.0	  0.0	  1.9</p>
<p> Other				  0.3	  0.1	  3.0</p>
<p>Note - In food, fresh food rose 0.4 pct from the previous month (down 1.1 pct year-on-year) and processed food fell 0.1 (down 0.3 pct year-on-year)</p>
</text>
